A||||1||Patrick's Dad||Carrying a Torch. -->||||1||
Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||12-28-2001||04:18 PM||||Third time's a charm, I guess. The Olympic Torch was supposed to be in Weymouth Landing somewhere between 1:00 - 1:30PM. At 12:55, we were stuck in traffic behind it. I detoured around it, figuring to get ahead of it at the Braintree/Quincy (QWIN-zee) line. They knew that we were coming, so they put it in a car and got ahead of us.<P>We finally caught up with it in Quincy Center, after some choice words that I hope my son didn't pick up on (He did admonish me for the word "stupid.").<P>Here is the torch being passed:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PassingTorch.jpg"> <P>Here is the torch heading up Hancock Street:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CarryingTorch.jpg"> <P>Afterwards, my family was happy to have witnessed an historic occasion, but even happier that it went quickly in windy 31° weather.||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||12-28-2001||11:36 PM||||Pretty cool!  (Literally)  I got to see the '96 torch as it came through Decatur, GA.  There hasn't been such a crowd in Decatur for 130 years.<P>||||reg||1
